WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:05.730
It takes a lot for a kid to steal the spotlight
from Deadpool, but Julian Dennison has a superhuman

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:06.730
amount of charisma.

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:11.360
A native of New Zealand, the young actor plays
Russell, the mysterious mutant at the center

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.480
of Deadpool 2.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:18.030
It's a huge role for Dennison, a self-proclaimed
Marvel movie fan, but it's far from his first.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:22.269
He's been in critically acclaimed indie flicks,
hugely popular viral videos, and one of the

00:00:22.269 --> 00:00:25.859
most legitimately entertaining body spray
commercials ever made.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:29.320
Here's why the kid from Deadpool 2 looks so
familiar.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.509
Shopping

00:00:30.509 --> 00:00:34.160
Dennison was just a shy student from the suburbs
of New Zealand when the filmmakers for the

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.210
coming-of-age film Shopping came to his school,
looking for a young actor to star in the film.

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:42.949
Dennison's mom told Stuff that the filmmakers
narrowed down the search to Dennison or his

00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:44.489
twin brother Christian.

00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:49.380
The film premiered at the Sundance Film Festival
in 2013 and instantly turned Dennison into

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.609
a local celebrity.

00:00:50.609 --> 00:00:54.809
He won Best Supporting Actor at the New Zealand
Film Awards, and credits the experience with

00:00:54.809 --> 00:00:56.890
making him want to become an actor.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:57.940
Blazed

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:02.850
Dennison's debut in Shopping didn't just impress
the critics, it also brought him one incredibly

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:09.030
important fan: Taika Waititi, the Oscar-nominated
director of the 2004 short film Two Cars,

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:12.450
One Night who would eventually go on to helm
Thor: Ragnarok.

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:16.930
Waititi thought Dennison would be perfect
for his next project: an extended public service

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:20.360
announcement about the dangers of driving
under the influence of marijuana.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:24.439
The two-minute video for the New Zealand Transport
Agency features three kids who imitate the

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:28.160
antics of their stoned fathers behind the
wheel of a car.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.180
"It's too fast!

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.020
It's too fast!

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.960
Take the wheel I'm freaking out!"

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:40.860
Dennison is hilarious throughout much of the
clip, but he also shows a hint of depth in

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.280
the final moments.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.460
The commercial became a viral sensation and
generated headlines around the world.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.980
"I love this music."

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.480
"What music?"

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:56.780
It also created a bond between Waititi and
Dennison that would yield another successful

00:01:56.799 --> 00:01:58.840
collaboration down the road.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.009
Paper Planes

00:02:00.009 --> 00:02:03.780
Dennison's next appearance on the big screen
came courtesy of a supporting role in the

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:08.350
family drama Paper Planes, an uplifting tale
about a young boy in Australia who dreams

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:12.250
of competing in the World Paper Plane Championships
in Japan.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:17.520
Dennison plays Kevin, a school bully who eventually
becomes the best friend of the main character.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.480
Acclaimed Australian director Robert Connolly
co-wrote and directed the film with an impressive

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.690
cast that includes Sam Worthington.

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:27.850
While the movie performed well at the Australian
box office, it was far less successful in

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:29.310
the rest of the world.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:32.850
Still, critics couldn't help but notice Dennison,
even in a smaller role.

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:37.330
The New Zealand Herald said he turned in a
"scene-stealing performance" as the reformed

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:38.440
bully Kevin.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:41.480
"It doesn't get much closer than that."

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:44.340
Hunt for the Wilderpeople

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:49.620
If you recognize Dennison from anything prior
to Deadpool 2, it's most likely Hunt for the

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:53.950
Wilderpeople, the heartwarming comedy that
served as his official breakthrough.

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:57.900
Writer and director Taika Waititi didn't even
make the young actor audition for the role

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:02.950
of Ricky Baker, a juvenile delinquent taken
to live on a remote farm with a loving foster

00:03:02.950 --> 00:03:04.760
mother and her cranky husband Hector.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:06.440
"You can't read?

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:10.540
You're like one of those people who are like
raised by like wolves or something.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:12.020
Hey, what's this?

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:12.900
This is woods.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:14.700
Me stupid."

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:19.290
After a sudden tragedy leads Ricky to ineptly
attempt to fake his own death, he and Hector

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:22.970
go on the run into the New Zealand bush and
become the targets of a comical manhunt.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:23.970
"S--- just got real.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:31.280
Back up homies, and let go of my uncle."

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.790
Dennison took a month away from school to
work on the movie, but it was definitely worth

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:35.790
it.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:39.400
Hunt for the Wilderpeople premiered at the
Sundance Film Festival and became the top-grossing

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.390
New Zealand film of all time.

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:44.920
It also directly paved the way for Dennison's
part in Deadpool 2.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:48.450
Ryan Reynolds told The New Zealand Herald
the casting was partly a result of his friendship

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:53.740
with Waititi, who co-starred with Reynolds
in 2011's Green Lantern.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:54.740
#YouGotSprung

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:58.260
After Hunt for the Wilderpeople made Dennison
one of the most recognizable people in New

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:01.920
Zealand, he put his star power to good use
in a completely unexpected way.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:06.980
In 2016, he teamed with Air New Zealand for
a clip to celebrate the start of spring and

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:08.930
Random Acts of Kindness Day.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:13.240
In a sort of Kiwi version of "pay it forward,"
Dennison traveled around the country to surprise

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.480
unsuspecting people with thoughtful gestures.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:18.870
"I'm like Santa Claus, but in spring."

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:22.910
In the clip, Dennison pays for people's meals
at a restaurant, takes flowers and chocolates

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.520
to patients in a hospital, and gives out free
ice cream.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:31.150
"So another awesome idea of ours to put a
spring back into someone's step is to throw

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.150
a banger ass party."

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:36.690
He ends the video by calling on New Zealanders
to surprise others with kindness, and we'd

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:40.530
be shocked if he didn't inspire at least a
few to do just that.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.200
Chronesthesia

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:46.470
About four months after Hunt for the Wilderpeople
hit theaters in New Zealand, Dennison returned

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:50.680
to the big screen for a small role in a very
different type of movie: he played Beni in

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:53.790
the indie time travel romance Chronesthesia.

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:58.490
The film was made in Wellington, New Zealand
with next to no budget and a bare bones crew.

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:02.931
Chronesthesia premiered at the New Zealand
International Film Festival in 2016, but it

00:05:02.931 --> 00:05:06.010
largely flew under the radar in America.

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:07.300
Summer Wonderland

00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:12.340
In late 2016, Dennison showed up in another
video for Air New Zealand, and this time he

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:13.750
had a noteworthy pal.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:17.900
In "Summer Wonderland," Dennison shows up
in a recording studio where Irish pop star

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:21.850
Ronan Keating is recording a take on the holiday
classic "Winter Wonderland."

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:25.070
But Keating doesn't make it past the second
line before Dennison interrupts.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:27.200
"I'm gonna stop you there, Roman."

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.020
"Ronan…"

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.580
"it doesn't really snow down here at Christmas,
so…"

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:34.470
Keating eventually walks out, but the pair
soon work out a new version of the song that's

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:36.040
more appropriate for the climate.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:39.890
Keating said in a press release that he signed
on for the project because he's a "big fan"

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:43.070
of New Zealand, but he also loved collaborating
with Dennison.

00:05:43.070 --> 00:05:44.070
He said:

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:45.920
"Working with Julian was a breeze.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:52.040
He's an absolute legend, incredibly professional,
and to top it off, he can definitely sing."

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:56.520
(singing)

00:05:57.720 --> 00:05:59.280
LYNX Australia

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:03.160
If you want a video to go viral, it's become
increasingly clear that Dennison should be

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:04.160
involved.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:08.780
The people at LYNX body spray must have known
this, and in early 2018, they teamed with

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:12.380
him for an extended commercial for their "Australia"
fragrance.

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:16.460
In the commercial, Dennison plays Humphrey,
a kid who doesn't have the best luck with

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:19.560
the ladies while his older brother Darius
is good at everything.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.570
"He's just so chill and confident.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:23.590
He can even talk to girls.

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:25.580
Strange behavior for a Kiwi, you know."

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:29.110
Darius eventually reveals his secret is LYNX
Australia.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:33.680
The ad ran on TV and before movies in theaters
in Australia, but it reached audiences around

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.430
the world when it hit the internet.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:41.080
Less than three months after it was released,
the ad had millions of views on YouTube.

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.260
"This was a bad idea."

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:47.700
Thanks for watching!

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:50.170
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:52.410
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

